# tools/crypto_bip39_mnemonic_witness.rish — BIP-39 entropy↔mnemonic authored in pure Rye, authoring NO new cryptography. The wallet arc's
# OTHER half, the one crypto/bip39_seed.rye explicitly left as "its own separate rung": the birth and the check of the backup phrase itself.
# from_entropy turns raw entropy into the twelve-to-twenty-four English words a keeper writes down; to_entropy reads a written phrase back to
# its entropy WHILE verifying the checksum — the guard that catches a mistyped backup word before it grows a wrong wallet (crypto · Season G).
#
# Season: crypto — Season G (the Six-Season double-seat). This rung contributes only BIP-39's word encoding — a CS = ENT/32 checksum from the
# GREEN crypto/sha256.rye and pure 11-bit bit-packing over BIP-39's fixed 2048-word English list — over stones already proven byte-for-byte on
# metal. Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md (Season G · the crypto parity wave).
# Clean-room: BIP-39 and its English word list are a public standard; the list is embedded byte-exact and hash-pinned, the assembly is ours,
# standing on our own parity-GREEN SHA-256, never a copied line (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# Parity is proven at selftest the replayable way the tree favours — the embedded 2048-word list is proven authentic (SHA-256 of the whole
# embedded table equals the published canonical digest 2f5eed53…3b24dbda, so a one-word tamper goes RED), then against BIP-39's OWN published
# Trezor vectors (English, fetched byte-exact from the canonical trezor/python-mnemonic vectors, never recited): six entropy values across all
# three published ENT lengths (128/192/256 bits → 12/18/24 words), both extremes each, encode to EXACTLY their published mnemonics word-for-word
# and decode back to EXACTLY their entropy byte-for-byte with the checksum verified. A flipped word is REFUSED InvalidChecksum; bad length,
# unknown word, and bad count each raise their named error. Purely local — every entropy is TEST entropy from the spec's own vectors, no
# network, no funds; generating real entropy and signing a real wallet stays the custody gate.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/crypto_bip39_mnemonic_witness.rish

say "crypto-bip39-mnemonic: Language EN — BIP-39 entropy↔mnemonic: the wallet arc's other half, the birth and the check of the backup phrase itself. from_entropy turns raw entropy into the twelve-to-twenty-four English words a keeper writes down; to_entropy reads a written phrase back to its entropy while verifying the checksum. Authors no new cryptography: one already-GREEN hash (SHA-256, crypto/sha256.rye) for the CS = ENT/32 checksum, plus pure 11-bit bit-packing over BIP-39's fixed 2048-word English list. This is the rung crypto/bip39_seed.rye named as its own — together they make BIP-39 whole in our Rye: entropy → mnemonic → seed → the HD tree crypto/bip32.rye grows."
say "crypto-bip39-mnemonic: Style Radiant — a keeper writes down twelve or twenty-four words, and this rung both makes them from entropy and, when a keeper types them back, catches a single mistyped word before it ever grows a wrong wallet. One list, one checksum, and the whole human edge of the backup phrase authored in the open and proven against the standard's own answers."
say "crypto-bip39-mnemonic: Lens TAME — every width named (2048-word list, 11-bit index, entropy 16..32 bytes, mnemonic bounded), contract asserts on the bit-packing and the exact (ENT+CS)/11 word count, a binary search bounded at 11 compares; it calls no cryptography of its own, only the GREEN SHA-256 beneath. The embedded word list is proven authentic against the published SHA-256, then parity holds against BIP-39's OWN published Trezor vectors: six entropy values across ENT 128/192/256 and both extremes encode to EXACTLY their published mnemonics word-for-word and decode back byte-for-byte with the checksum verified. A flipped word is refused InvalidChecksum; bad length, unknown word, and bad count each raise their named error. Purely local — TEST entropy only, no real identity key, no network, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "crypto/bin/bip39_mnemonic"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p crypto/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build crypto/bip39_mnemonic.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "crypto-bip39-mnemonic: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "crypto/bin/bip39_mnemonic.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "crypto-bip39-mnemonic: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "crypto-bip39-mnemonic: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN crypto-bip39-mnemonic' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "crypto-bip39-mnemonic: selftest did not print the GREEN crypto-bip39-mnemonic line"
